text:
For this, you must have one verse (or two) that runs as follows:

I am a young man and I know no fear;
I am an old man and afraid to die!

She is all alone, and has been for years,

With no one to speak or listen to her:

For she was born without ears, nor eyes;

Nor lips to praise or mouth to curse;

He was an old man, and I had to stop him from digging up his garden!

He saw me coming, at least that's what he told my mother;
But as soon as I got there he started throwing soil into his mouth!

I would have been wise, I was too weak to hear
 The cry within me when the earth moved and sank away;
 But it is not for those that are strong alone;
 For where shall we find the strength to move our feet?

The magnet of creation, where lies?

In the depths, where worlds are created;

There love's sweet magnetism remains;

It binds us and joins everything there.

Yet I am not sick, but only want to die;

 Not that life’s worth dying for, if it is such as ours –
 The life we live now and every day till death,

 When we have nothing more to wish or dream about, when there remains no reason to go on living;
